{
  "title": "VideoFrameSource",
  "description": "An `HTMLVideoElement` as a FrameSource. Where the browser supports `requestVideoFrameCallback`, every presented frame advances revision, so a paused video uploads nothing. Elsewhere the revision follows the playback position, polled when it is read. Metadata, resize and seek events advance it as well, so dimension changes and seeks while paused reach the texture. The source does not own the element: destroying it removes its listeners and callbacks, and leaves playback alone.",
  "symbol": "VideoFrameSource",
